# map visits — the areas stood in and the ways gone by are recorded, and outlive the visit
#
# AreaVisits writes them to the location's saved state, and the location map draws from them. The
# Field–Rock Track runs past the Test Yard, so following it from the field to the rock records the
# yard as visited too, and the two neighbour ways the track follows as taken — a path is a walk past
# the areas between its ends, not a jump. Then the location is left and entered again: the scene is
# rebuilt from its factory on arrival, and the record must come back with it.
#
# FLAGS: --playground --skip-childhood --debug --seed 42 --no-encounters --auto-dialogue --location-type test --location-id 0 --start-area "Test Field" --period dawn --observe-only "Field–Rock Track"

wait
click menu New
wait mode ProtagonistCreation 20
click continue
wait mode WorldView 60
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60

# Where the visit opens is visited before anything is done; nothing else is.
expect-state map visited Test Field
expect-no-state map visited Test Rock
expect-no-state map taken

strategy succeed
goal follow_path
advance 12 180

click keyword 0
choose 0
choose 0
advance 12 180

click action 0
choose 0
advance 12 180
click continue
advance 12 180
expect-verb follow_path
expect Moved to: Test Rock

inspect map
expect-state map visited Test Rock
expect-state map visited Test Yard
expect-state map taken Field–Rock Track
expect-state map taken between Test Field and Test Yard
expect-state map taken between Test Rock and Test Yard
# The move was shown on the map: the party walked the track's own line, from card to card.
expect-state map walk from Test Field to Test Rock
expect-state map via=line
# The wood is off the path: neither visited nor any way to it taken.
expect-no-state map Test Wood
save roundtrip

# Leave, come back: a rebuilt scene, the same record.
observe none
click button
wait 60
advance 12 180
click button
wait mode WorldView 90
travel here
wait mode LocationInteraction 60
inspect map
expect-state map visited Test Yard
expect-state map visited Test Rock
expect-state map taken Field–Rock Track
expect-state map taken between Test Field and Test Yard
# What the observations took in is seen, and only that: the field's introduction named the Test Mud,
# the crossing to the wood, so the wood is seen without ever being stood in.
expect-state map seen Test Wood
quit
